West Central Jefferson County in central Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 545 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 341 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly in the advisory area. Up to 1 inch of rain has fallen.\n\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nTroublesome Creek, Cub Creek, Bear Creek, North Turkey Creek,\nBlue Creek and Bergen Creek. Additional rainfall amounts up to\n0.5 inches are expected over the area. This additional rain will\nresult in minor flooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nEvergreen, Kittredge and Wah Keeney Park.","ends":"2026-09-25T17:45:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Jefferson, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f8253240ab4134ce80abd175e5b3c3719a66d70f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f8253240ab4134ce80abd175e5b3c3719a66d70f.001.1"},{"event":"Special Weather Statement","headline":"Special Weather Statement issued September 25 at 3:36PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"At 336 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a line of strong\nthunderstorms extending from near Rocky Flats to near Tiny Town, or\nextending from 20 miles northwest of Denver to 19 miles southwest of\nDenver, moving east at 15 mph.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts up to 40 mph and half inch size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around\nunsecured objects. Minor damage to outdoor objects is\npossible.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nWestern Denver, Lakewood, southwestern Thornton, Arvada,\nWestminster, southwestern Broomfield, northwestern Highlands Ranch,\nLittleton, Northglenn, Englewood, Wheat Ridge, Golden, Federal\nHeights, Sheridan, Morrison, Red Rocks Park, Idledale, Indian Hills\nand Tiny Town.","ends":"2026-09-25T16:15:00-06:00","severity":"Moderate","areaDesc":"Jeffers